flat.", "Watch": "Watch for children who might submerge the boat completely. Remind them to place it gently flat on top of the water.", "Phases": [{"Name": "The Sail Fold", "ChildrenDo": "Fold the square paper in half corner-to-corner to create a large triangle sail shape.", "TeacherDoes": "Demonstrates the fold, encouraging children to press hard along the folded edge to make a sharp crease.", "DurationMinutes": 5}, {"Name": "The Boat Hull Fold", "ChildrenDo": "Fold the bottom pointy corner of the triangle upward to create a flat, horizontal bottom edge (the boat's hull).", "TeacherDoes": "Assists children with this fold, showing how it creates a flat base that allows the boat to stand up.", "DurationMinutes": 5}, {"Name": "Waterproofing with Wax", "ChildrenDo": "Color the bottom fold of the boat heavily with wax crayons to coat the paper.", "TeacherDoes": "Explains how the wax crayon acts like an umbrella, keeping the water away from the paper.", "DurationMinutes": 7}, {"Name": "The Float Test", "ChildrenDo": "Gently place their sailboat in the water tray and watch it float. Place a tiny plastic toy inside the fold.", "TeacherDoes": "Monitors the water play, encouraging children to gently blow on the sails to make their boats move.", "DurationMinutes": 8}], "Safety": ["Keep water depth very shallow (no more than 2-3 cm).", "Have towels ready to immediately wipe up any water spills on the floor to prevent slipping."], "Closing": "Help children rescue their boats from the water, dry them gently with a towel, and place them on a tray to take home.", "Extensions": ["Add a drop of blue food coloring to the water trays to make a realistic ocean.", "Use a straw to blow air and race the boats across the water tray."], "Adaptations": ["For younger children, use thicker pre-waxed paper (like patty wrappers) that is easier to fold and naturally waterproof.", "For older children, challenge them to fold a double-sail boat by folding both side corners upward."], "Preparation": 