 giant windstorm? Where is your animal passenger sailing to, and what is their favorite silly song to sing while riding the waves?", "Try": "Try rubbing your crayon back and forth as fast as a racing car to make the shiny wax armor super-thick and shiny!", "Watch": "Watch for over-excited captains blowing bubbles so hard they splash water out of the tray, or accidentally sucking in instead of blowing. Keep an eye out for dry papers that need extra scribble-armor before launching.", "Phases": [{"Name": "Origami Gymnastics", "ChildrenDo": "Fold the square corner-to-corner to make a triangle, wear it as a silly hat, then fold the bottom up to make a secret pocket.", "TeacherDoes": "Guides the steps with funny sound effects, checking that everyone wears their paper hat and giggles before moving to the pocket fold.", "DurationMinutes": 5}, {"Name": "Scribble Tag!", "ChildrenDo": "Scribble as fast as possible with wax crayons to cover the entire bottom of their boat in thick 'wax armor'.", "TeacherDoes": "Plays upbeat music and calls out challenge styles: 'Scribble like a slow turtle! Now scribble like a speedy rocket! No white spots left!'", "DurationMinutes": 7}, {"Name": "The Bubble Rodeo Launch", "ChildrenDo": "Tuck their animal toy into the pocket, blow through their straws to create bubbles in the tray, then blow their boat across the soapy waves to an island.", "TeacherDoes": "Acts as the Co-Captain, cheering them on, making dramatic wind noises, and helping them guide their boats to safety.", "DurationMinutes": 8}], "Safety": ["Ensure children only blow OUT of the straws and do not drink the soapy blue water.", "Keep dry towels handy to immediately wipe up any soapy slips on the floor."], "Closing": "Have captains park their boats, tuck their animal toys into warm towel 'sleeping bags' to dry off, and do a synchronized victory wiggle!", "Extensions": ["Have a 'Silly Sailing Race' where kids try to blow their boats to touch three different sponge islands in a row.", "Add a splash of yellow paint to the sponge islands and see if they can make 'green foam' when their blue-water boats crash land!"], "Adaptations": ["For younger sailors, use pre-folded paper boats so they can focus entirely on the fun of scribbling and blowing bubbles.", "For older captains, let them tape two straws together to make a 'double-barreled wind blaster' for extra sailing power."], "Preparation": ["Fill shallow trays with 2cm of water, add blue food coloring, and add a generous squeeze of dish soap.", "Place a few kitchen sponges in the trays to act as floating islands."], "MaterialSetup": ["Set out piles of square paper and baskets of chunky crayons. Keep the straws and soapy water trays covered with towels like 'mystery fog' until launch time."], "EnvironmentSetup": ["Create 'Scribble Port' tables for folding/coloring and 'The Bubble Ocean' tables for the watery launch zones."], "TeacherIntroduction": "Ahoy, Goofy Captains! The Bubble Monster is tickling the ocean and making giant bubbly waves! We need to make magic scribble-boats, load up our goofy animal buddies, and blow a giant windstorm to sail them to safety. Who is ready to make some waves?", "LittleMomentOpportunity": "Capturing the pure joy and bubbly cheeks of a child blowing a huge mound of blue bubbles in their tray to create a safe harbor for their toy animal.", "SuggestedDurationMinutes": 25}, "TeacherGuidance": "Bring high-energy theatrical play! Use a playful pirate/sea-captain voice, make silly sound effects (swoosh, pop, splash!), and frame the crayon-coloring step as a speedy race game to keep engagement sky-high.", "DevelopmentalGoals": []}	Draft Saved	df5d8828-f7cb-4250-9cd1-dba1d787d531	2026-10-09 12:14:53.711815+00
d21b20eb-a984-4bdc-a6ac-6a3915773886	ab1835e9-e86e-476b-9c2d-3c4a814d21c1	1	New Experience	Start crafting a wonderful day for the children.	{}	Initial Creation	df5d8828-f7cb-4250-9cd1-dba1d787d531	2026-10-09 13:07:30.210385+00
6fe10220-ce02-41be-a3f7-35c09cc1b085	3a48a470-63cd-492c-ba6f-8dd3032205cf	13	Scribble-Sailors' Giggly Bubble-Pop Rodeo!	A wild, high-sensory water adventure where kids transform paper into wobbly boats with 'crayon-armor', choose a goofy toy animal buddy, and blow through straws to create a mountain of giggly bubbles to save their friend from the Tickle Monster!	{"AgeMax": 4, "AgeMin": 3, "Create": "Scribble a super-thick layer of colorful crayon wax onto your paper boat, pop your goofy toy passenger into its cozy seat, and blow a storm of bubbles to sail your ship safely to Sponge Island!", "Together": "We will wiggle our toes like seaweed, wear our paper boats as funny hats, scribble-tickle our papers with giant crayons, and blow a colossal mountain of blue bubbles!", "Challenge": "Can you give your paper boat super-shiny wax armor to protect your goofy animal buddy from the Tickle Monster's massive bubble-storm?", "Materials": ["Square paper (15cm x 15cm)", "Chunky wax crayons", "Shallow plastic trays", "Blue dish soap water", "Small toy animals", "Colorful kitchen sponges", "Drinking straws"], "Reflection": "What sound did your boat make when it crashed into the bubble mountain? Did your animal passenger get their toes wet?", "ChildChoice": "Children choose their own goofy toy passenger, pick their favorite 'speedy' crayon colors, name their boat something silly (like 'Captain Cupcake'), and choose which color sponge island to crash-land onto.", "Environment": "Indoor / Outdoor", "MagicMoment": "The instant of pure magic when children blow through their straws, creating a towering, wobbling mountain of blue bubbles that overflows the tray and tickles their noses!", "GroupSizeMax": 10, "GroupSizeMin": 4, "Accomplishment": "Rescuing their silly animal friend from the tickle-storm and parking their boat on a squishy, wet sponge island with a victory cheer!", "ExecutionGuide": {"Ask": "What is your animal friend's favorite silly song to sing while riding the giant bubble waves, and what sound does your boat make when it hits a bubble?", "Try": "Try rubbing your crayon back and forth as fast as a racing car to make the shiny wax armor super thick so the water can't tickle your boat's tummy!", "Watch": "Watch for eager captains who try to drink the soapy water instead of blowing; remind them we are blowing 'wind' OUT, not sipping juice IN! Also watch for soggy paper boats that need a quick crayon touch-up.", "Phases": [{"Name": "Silly Hat Ceremony", "ChildrenDo": "Fold paper into a simple boat/hat, wear it on their heads, and make funny boat noises (like 'chugga-chugga-toot-toot!').", "TeacherDoes": "Guides the folding with funny sound effects and takes a mental 'captain photo' of everyone wearing their hats.", "DurationMinutes": 5}, {"Name": "The Scribble-Tickle!", "ChildrenDo": "Scribble as fast and hard as they can with wax crayons to coat the paper bottom with shiny wax.", "TeacherDoes": "Plays fast music and calls out silly styles: 'Scribble like a wobbly penguin! Scribble like a happy puppy!'", "DurationMinutes": 7}, {"Name": "Bubble-Pop Rodeo", "ChildrenDo": "Load their animal toy into the boat, place the boat in the tray, and blow through straws to create a giant bubble storm, guiding their boat to the sponge island.", "TeacherDoes": "Acts as the storm coordinator, cheering on the captains as they blow huge soapy mountains and make loud wind noises.", "DurationMinutes": 8}], "Safety": ["Ensure children only blow OUT of the straws and do not sip the soapy water.", "Keep towels nearby to immediately wipe up any soapy spills on the floor."], "Closing": "Have all captains park their ships, give their animal toys a warm towel hug, and perform a synchronized 'wobbly seaweed dance' to celebrate!", "Extensions": ["Create a 'Bubble-Pop Symphony' where children try to pop as many bubbles as they can using only their noses!", "Add a drop of yellow paint to the sponge islands and watch the blue bubble water turn green when they crash land!"], "Adaptations": ["For younger children, pre-fold the boats so they can dive straight into the fun of scribbling and bubble blowing.", "For older kids, let them use two straws at once to create a 'double turbo' wind blaster."], "Preparation": ["Mix water, blue food coloring, and dish soap in the trays.", "Cut sponges into funny cloud shapes to make 'Sponge Islands' and place them in the trays."], "MaterialSetup": ["Place crayons in baskets, stack the square papers, and hide the water trays under towels like 'secret oceans' until the big reveal."], "EnvironmentSetup": ["Set up a 'Scribble Shipyard' table for coloring and a 'Bubble Ocean' area for water play."], "TeacherIntroduction": "Ahoy, Captains! I am Captain Barnacle-Belly! A giant, ticklish Bubble Monster is coming to tickle our toes! We must build scribble-armored ships, grab our silly animal sidekicks, and blow a massive bubble defense shield! Who is ready to get silly?", "LittleMomentOpportunity": "Catching the wide-eyed, giggling face of a child covered in tiny blue bubbles as they successfully blow their boat all the way to Sponge Island.", "SuggestedDurationMinutes": 25}, "TeacherGuidance": "Go full cartoon character! Use a silly pirate voice, wear a paper hat, make exaggerated gasping sounds when the bubbles grow, and keep the energy soaring by treating every scribble like a race against the Tickle Monster.", "DevelopmentalGoals": []}	Draft Saved	df5d8828-f7cb-4250-9cd1-dba1d787d531	2026-10-09 13:25:02.274866+00
63d66b1c-d6f2-48a5-8c29-d3db586299c4	3a48a470-63cd-492c-ba6f-8dd3032205cf	14	The Wobbly, Bubbly Scribble-Ship Circus!	A highly interactive, laughter-packed water adventure where children transform paper into bouncy circus boats with colorful crayon armor, choose a silly squeaky animal buddy, and blow a towering mountain of blue giggling bubbles to build a protective shield against the ticklish Bubble Monster!	{"AgeMax": 4, "AgeMin": 3, "Create": "Decorate your paper boat with a super-thick layer of colorful crayon wax, pop your silly animal buddy inside, and blow a wild storm of bubbles to guide your ship to a safe, squishy sponge island!", "Together": "We will do the 'seaweed-wiggle' dance, wear our paper boats as goofy hats, scribble at lightning-fast speed, and blow a colossal, wobbly mountain of blue bubbles!", "Challenge": "Can you give your wobbly paper boat a shiny coat of magic crayon armor to keep your ticklish squeaky-animal passenger safe from the giant giggle-bubble storm?", "Materials": ["Square colorful paper (15cm x 15cm)", "Chunky wax crayons", "Shallow plastic trays", "Soapy water with blue food coloring", "Small squeaky toy animals", "Colorful kitchen sponges cut into fun shapes", "Drinking straws"], "Reflection": "What funny sound did your animal friend make when the bubbles tickled their toes? What was your boat's favorite dance move today?", "ChildChoice": "Children choose their own squeaky animal passenger, pick their favorite neon crayon colors, decide on a goofy name for their ship, and choose which shaped sponge island to park on.", "Environment": "Indoor / Outdoor", "MagicMoment": "The explosive laughter when the blue bubbles grow so tall they spill over the tray and land on the children's noses, giving them instant 'bubble mustaches'!", "GroupSizeMax": 10, "GroupSizeMin": 4, "Accomplishment": "Successfully rescuing their animal buddy from the tickle-storm and giving their partner a high-five using a squishy, wet sponge!", "ExecutionGuide": {"Ask": "What silly sound does your animal buddy make when a bubble tickles their tummy, and what is the name of your boat's favorite dance move?", "Try": "Try holding your crayon like a magic wand and scribble-scribbling as fast as a zooming rocket to make your boat's shiny wax armor super-strong!", "Watch": "Watch for silly sailors who might try to sip the soapy bubble juice through their straws; playfully show them how to blow 'birthday candle' winds OUT, and keep an eye out for ultra-soggy paper bottoms that need extra crayon scribbles!", "Phases": [{"Name": "Silly Captain Parade", "ChildrenDo": "Fold their paper into a simple boat shape, place it on their heads like a funny hat, and march in place making goofy engine noises.", "TeacherDoes": "Guides the folding using silly names for the folds ('hot dog fold', 'bouncy triangle fold') and snaps imaginary silly photos of the children's hat styles.", "DurationMinutes": 5}, {"Name": "The Scribble-Race Frenzy", "ChildrenDo": "Scribble-color the bottom of their paper boat as fast as they can with wax crayons to make it waterproof.", "TeacherDoes": "Plays fast, goofy circus music and calls out silly coloring styles: 'Color like a hyper monkey! Color like a slow-motion sloth!'", "DurationMinutes": 7}, {"Name": "The Bubble-Pop Circus", "ChildrenDo": "Place their squeaky toy in their boat, set it in the water tray, and blow through their straws to create a giant, foaming mountain of blue bubbles to float their boat to the sponge island.", "TeacherDoes": "Leads a dramatic 'bubble-blowing countdown' and cheers loudly as the bubbles grow, pointing out who has the tallest bubble mountain or the best bubble mustache.", "DurationMinutes": 13}], "Safety": ["Remind children continuously to only blow OUT, never suck IN through the straws.", "Keep plenty of dry towels handy to mop up any slippery soapy splashes on the floor immediately."], "Closing": "Lead all captains in parking their boats, giving their squeaky toys a warm towel-blanket tuck-in, and doing a giant group 'Wobbly Seaweed Dance' to celebrate their success!", "Extensions": ["Have a 'Bubble Nose-Pop' game where kids try to pop the tallest bubble using only the tip of their nose without touching it with their hands!", "Add a drop of red paint to the sponge islands to watch the blue bubble water magically swirl into purple when they arrive!"], "Adaptations": ["For younger children, pre-fold the boats so they can jump straight into the coloring and bubble-blowing play.", "For older kids, challenge them to build a 'bubble bridge' across the tray using two straws at the same time."], "Preparation": ["Mix water, blue food coloring, and plenty of dish soap in the plastic trays.", "Cut colorful sponges into star, cloud, or heart shapes to act as 'Silly Sponge Islands' and place them inside the trays."], "MaterialSetup": ["Place crayons in bright baskets, stack the square paper, and cover the water trays with colorful towels to make the 'Big Bubble Reveal' exciting."], "EnvironmentSetup": ["Create a 'Silly Shipyard' coloring table with bright decorations and a nearby 'Bubbly Ocean Arena' for the water play trays."], "TeacherIntroduction": "Welcome to the Bubbly Scribble-Ship Circus! I am your Ringleader! A giant, ticklish Bubble Monster is tickling our toes! We need to make shiny, crayon-armored circus boats, grab our squeakiest animal friends, and blow a huge, wobbly shield of blue bubbles to protect them! Who is ready to get silly?", "LittleMomentOpportunity": "The pure joy when a child successfully blows a bubble dome so big that it completely encapsulates their little toy animal passenger, leading to gasps and giggles.", "SuggestedDurationMinutes": 25}, "TeacherGuidance": "Become a cartoon character! Wear a silly hat, use funny sound effects (whoosh, pop, boing), make giant cartoonish facial expressions, and treat every step like an exciting, playful game.", "DevelopmentalGoals": []}	Draft Saved	df5d8828-f7cb-4250-9cd1-dba1d787d531	2026-10-09 13:26:03.279633+00
