 {"Ask": "What silly sound does your animal buddy make when a bubble tickles their tummy, and what is the name of your boat's favorite dance move?", "Try": "Try holding your crayon like a magic wand and scribble-scribbling as fast as a zooming rocket to make your boat's shiny wax armor super-strong!", "Watch": "Watch for silly sailors who might try to sip the soapy bubble juice through their straws; playfully show them how to blow 'birthday candle' winds OUT, and keep an eye out for ultra-soggy paper bottoms that need extra crayon scribbles!", "Phases": [{"Name": "The Scribble-Race Frenzy", "ChildrenDo": "Scribble-color the bottom of their paper boat as fast as they can with wax crayons to make it waterproof.", "TeacherDoes": "Plays fast, goofy circus music and calls out silly coloring styles: 'Color like a hyper monkey! Color like a slow-motion sloth!'", "DurationMinutes": 7}, {"Name": "The Bubble-Pop Circus", "ChildrenDo": "Place their squeaky toy in their boat, set it in the water tray, and blow through their straws to create a giant, foaming mountain of blue bubbles to float their boat to the sponge island.", "TeacherDoes": "Leads a dramatic 'bubble-blowing countdown' and cheers loudly as the bubbles grow, pointing out who has the tallest bubble mountain or the best bubble mustache.", "DurationMinutes": 13}, {"Name": "Silly Captain Parade", "ChildrenDo": "Fold their paper into a simple boat shape, place it on their heads like a funny hat, and march in place making goofy engine noises.", "TeacherDoes": "Guides the folding using silly names for the folds ('hot dog fold', 'bouncy triangle fold') and snaps imaginary silly photos of the children's hat styles.", "DurationMinutes": 5}], "Safety": ["Remind children continuously to only blow OUT, never suck IN through the straws.", "Keep plenty of dry towels handy to mop up any slippery soapy splashes on the floor immediately."], "Closing": "Lead all captains in parking their boats, giving their squeaky toys a warm towel-blanket tuck-in, and doing a giant group 'Wobbly Seaweed Dance' to celebrate their success!", "Extensions": ["Have a 'Bubble Nose-Pop' game where kids try to pop the tallest bubble using only the tip of their nose without touching it with their hands!", "Add a drop of red paint to the sponge islands to watch the blue bubble water magically swirl into purple when they arrive!"], "Adaptations": ["For younger children, pre-fold the boats so they can jump straight into the coloring and bubble-blowing play.", "For older kids, challenge them to build a 'bubble bridge' across the tray using two straws at the same time."], "Preparation": ["Mix water, blue food coloring, and plenty of dish soap in the plastic trays.", "Cut colorful sponges into star, cloud, or heart shapes to act as 'Silly Sponge Islands' and place them inside the trays."], "MaterialSetup": ["Place crayons in bright baskets, stack the square paper, and cover the water trays with colorful towels to make the 'Big Bubble Reveal' exciting."], "EnvironmentSetup": ["Create a 'Silly Shipyard' coloring table with bright decorations and a nearby 'Bubbly Ocean Arena' for the water play trays."], "TeacherIntroduction": "Welcome to the Bubbly Scribble-Ship Circus! I am your Ringleader! A giant, ticklish Bubble Monster is tickling our toes! We need to make shiny, crayon-armored circus boats, grab our squeakiest animal friends, and blow a huge, wobbly shield of blue bubbles to protect them! Who is ready to get silly?", "LittleMomentOpportunity": "The pure joy when a child successfully blows a bubble dome so big that it completely encapsulates their little toy animal passenger, leading to gasps and giggles.", "SuggestedDurationMinutes": 25}, "TeacherGuidance": "Become a cartoon character! Wear a silly hat, use funny sound effects (whoosh, pop, boing), make giant cartoonish facial expressions, and treat every step like an exciting, playful game.", "DevelopmentalGoals": []}	Draft Saved	df5d8828-f7cb-4250-9cd1-dba1d787d531	2026-10-09 13:54:07.231467+00
