 {"Ask": "What silly sound does your animal buddy make when a bubble tickles their tummy, and what is the name of your boat's favorite dance move?", "Try": "Try holding your crayon like a magic wand and scribble-scribbling as fast as a zooming rocket to make your boat's shiny wax armor super-strong!", "Watch": "Watch for silly sailors who might try to sip the soapy bubble juice through their straws; playfully show them how to blow 'birthday candle' winds OUT, and keep an eye out for ultra-soggy paper bottoms that need extra crayon scribbles!", "Phases": [{"Name": "The Scribble-Race Frenzy", "ChildrenDo": "Scribble-color the bottom of their paper boat as fast as they can with wax crayons to make it waterproof.", "TeacherDoes": "Plays fast, goofy circus music and calls out silly coloring styles: 'Color like a hyper monkey! Color like a slow-motion sloth!'", "DurationMinutes": 7}, {"Name": "The Bubble-Pop Circus", "ChildrenDo": "Place their squeaky toy in their boat, set it in the water tray, and blow through their straws to create a giant, foaming mountain of blue bubbles to float their boat to the sponge island.", "TeacherDoes": "Leads a dramatic 'bubble-blowing countdown' and cheers loudly as the bubbles grow, pointing out who has the tallest bubble mountain or the best bubble mustache.", "DurationMinutes": 13}, {"Name": "Silly Captain Parade", "ChildrenDo": "Fold their paper into a simple boat shape, place it on their heads like a funny hat, and march in place making goofy engine noises.", "TeacherDoes": "Guides the folding using silly names for the folds ('hot dog fold', 'bouncy triangle fold') and snaps imaginary silly photos of the children's hat styles.", "DurationMinutes": 5}], "Safety": ["Remind children continuously to only blow OUT, never suck IN through the straws.", "Keep plenty of dry towels handy to mop up any slippery soapy splashes on the floor immediately."], "Closing": "Lead all captains in parking their boats, giving their squeaky toys a warm towel