an balance on one giant wiggly leg."], "Preparation": ["Roll the clay into round 'sleeping' balls.", "Bend several pipe cleaners into zig-zags and spirals.", "Hide the eyes, feathers, and pom-poms under plastic cups on each tray like secret surprise hats."], "MaterialSetup": ["Place a 'sleeping' ball of clay on each tray.", "Place the upside-down surprise cups next to the clay."], "EnvironmentSetup": ["Create a 'Monster Dance Floor' by taping a bright sheet of paper in the center of the table.", "Set up individual trays for each child to contain the playdough splats."], "TeacherIntroduction": "Shh... look! Our clay balls are fast asleep! On the count of three, let's give them a gentle tickle and shout 'WAKE UP, CLAY!' One, two, three... WAKE UP!", "LittleMomentOpportunity": "When a child puts an eye in a weird place like the bottom of the clay, dramatically pretend the monster is looking at your toes and giggle together about its 'toe-vision'.", "SuggestedDurationMinutes": 25}, "TeacherGuidance": "Keep the energy high and full of pretend play. Use your voice to bring the clay to life—giggle when you touch it, make 'boop' sounds when adding eyes, and encourage children to talk to their monsters. Focus on the joy of creation rather than making a perfect figure.", "DevelopmentalGoals": [], "_platformProvenance": {"Version": 1, "ImportedAt": "2026-10-15T22:06:46.4829443+00:00", "PlatformExperienceId": "b1395d93-9d90-4e64-9226-a1c201b651ce"}}	50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002	2026-10-15 22:06:46.490997+00	2026-10-15 22:06:46.490998+00	ee79a62a-90be-476a-a22a-cd4d8a2eaac2
